# xhci98.sys import allowlist (amd64) - the 64-bit build, held to NT 5.2
# amd64 evidence (winxp64-baselines.expected). A sibling file rather than a
# column in xhci98-imports.allow (the owner's decision, 2026-09-09): Windows 98
# is not a target of this binary, so the x86 file's Windows 98 denials do not
# transfer, and most XP-era APIs exist here.
#
# Since 2026-10-02 xhci98.sys is the successor HCD (design record 13); the
# gate's three HCD rules stated in xhci98-imports.allow - no USBPORT.SYS pair,
# an empty import table only while the scaffold marker is in the image, the
# pool family denied until its rows exist - apply here unchanged. Phase 28 task
# 28-A.2 is the amd64 build's own phase; until then this file grows in step
# with the x86 one.

[imports]

# Task 25.8's scaffold calls nothing. The amd64 image imports one pair the
# compiler adds rather than the source:
#
# --- The /GS stack cookie handler ------------------------------------------
# **Nothing in this driver calls KeBugCheckEx, and this row is not a licence to
# start.** WDK 7.1 enables /GS buffer security checks for amd64, so every
# function with a stack buffer gets a cookie check, and __security_check_cookie
# jumps to __report_gsfailure on a mismatch, which issues KeBugCheckEx(0xF7) =
# DRIVER_OVERRAN_STACK_BUFFER. Unreachable except on a genuine stack-buffer
# overrun, and a safety the x86 build (MSVC 6.0, pre-/GS) cannot have, which
# is why the row is accepted rather than the flag turned off. The miniport's
# amd64 file carried the same row from task 21.3. A second call site would be
# this driver's own and needs its own decision.
ntoskrnl.exe!KeBugCheckEx                 all  required  nt52-amd64-export (hint 213, ntoskrnl RVA 0x41690 / ntkrnlmp 0x2E950); /GS __report_gsfailure only, bugcheck 0xF7

# --- Task 26-A.1: the FDO's attach, PnP forwarding and power pass-through ---
# The amd64 twins of the x86 file's rows of the same task; NT 5.2 amd64's
# export table is the evidence, which the gate re-derives from
# winxp64-baselines.expected for every row. The Interlocked pair is a
# compiler intrinsic on amd64 and imports nothing.
ntoskrnl.exe!IoCreateDevice                all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoDeleteDevice                all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoAttachDeviceToDeviceStack   all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoDetachDevice                all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!IofCallDriver                 all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!IofCompleteRequest            all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeInitializeEvent             all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeSetEvent                    all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeWaitForSingleObject         all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!PoStartNextPowerIrp           all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!PoCallDriver                  all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!PoSetPowerState               all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.1)
# WDK 7.1's checked headers wrap the IRP stack-location macros
# (IoSkipCurrentIrpStackLocation and its siblings) in ASSERT, which the x86
# Windows 2000 DDK's do not, so the amd64 checked builds import RtlAssert and
# the x86 ones do not. Checked flavours only; no source calls it.
ntoskrnl.exe!RtlAssert                     debug  required  nt52-amd64-export; WDK 7.1 checked-header ASSERTs only (task 26-A.1)
ntoskrnl.exe!RtlAssert                     qemu   required  nt52-amd64-export; WDK 7.1 checked-header ASSERTs only (task 26-A.1)


# --- Task 26-A.2: the controller FDO. Twins of the x86 rows of the same task ---
# --- where amd64 imports the pair at all: the Interlocked, Kf* spin-lock and  ---
# --- IRQL, and register-accessor pairs are intrinsics or ntoskrnl inlines on   ---
# --- amd64, which instead imports KeAcquireSpinLockRaiseToDpc /               ---
# --- KeReleaseSpinLock for KeAcquireSpinLock/KeReleaseSpinLock.                 ---
ntoskrnl.exe!IoAllocateIrp                 all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoFreeIrp                     all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoConnectInterrupt            all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoDisconnectInterrupt         all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoOpenDeviceRegistryKey       all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeAcquireSpinLockRaiseToDpc   all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeReleaseSpinLock             all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeCancelTimer                 all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeClearEvent                  all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeDelayExecutionThread        all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeInitializeDpc               all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeInitializeTimer             all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeInsertQueueDpc              all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeRemoveQueueDpc              all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!KeSetTimer                    all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!MmMapIoSpace                  all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!MmUnmapIoSpace                all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!PoRequestPowerIrp             all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!PsCreateSystemThread          all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!PsTerminateSystemThread       all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!ObReferenceObjectByHandle    all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!ObfDereferenceObject         all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoIsWdmVersionAvailable      all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!ExQueueWorkItem               all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!RtlQueryRegistryValues        all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!ZwClose                       all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!IoGetDmaAdapter               all  required  SITES=hcd_dma.obj nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
HAL.dll!KeStallExecutionProcessor          all  required  nt52-amd64-export; twin of the x86 row (task 26-A.2)
ntoskrnl.exe!DbgPrint                      qemu required  nt52-amd64-export; the qemu flavour's live trace only (xhci_dbg.c), as on x86 (task 26-A.2)

[deny]

ExAllocatePool              Not the HCD's spelling (xhci98-imports.allow; task 25.3). Allocate with ExAllocatePoolWithTag once its row exists.
ExAllocatePoolWithTag       The HCD's allocation entry point once 26-A.1 / 28-A.2 add its row. Denied until then.
ExFreePool                  Same as ExAllocatePoolWithTag.
ExFreePoolWithTag           No Windows 98 evidence, and the x86 and amd64 sources are one tree: free with ExFreePool on both.
IoForwardIrpSynchronously   Windows XP and later - blocks the load on Win2000, and the x86 and amd64 sources are one tree. Use IoCallDriver plus a completion routine that signals a KEVENT.
IoSetCompletionRoutineEx    Windows XP and later - blocks the load on Win2000, as above.
IoCsqInitialize             Cancel-safe queues arrived with the XP DDK and are not in the Win2K DDK's libraries.
IoCsqInsertIrp              Cancel-safe queue family - not in the Win2K DDK.
IoCsqRemoveNextIrp          Cancel-safe queue family - not in the Win2K DDK.
